Niri maps every libinput touch/tablet device to one fallback output
(input.touch.map-to-output / input.tablet.map-to-output). Dual touchscreens
therefore both land on the same monitor.

This makes Device::output() honor udev WL_OUTPUT (libinput's output_name)
so each digitizer can target its own DRM connector. Devices without
WL_OUTPUT still use the config fallback.

Deck udev rules live in hosts/deck/nixos/system.nix.

--- a/src/input/backend_ext.rs
+++ b/src/input/backend_ext.rs
@@ -24,8 +24,8 @@
 }
 
 impl NiriInputDevice for libinput::Device {
-    fn output(&self, _state: &State) -> Option<Output> {
-        // FIXME: Allow specifying the output per-device?
-        None
+    fn output(&self, state: &State) -> Option<Output> {
+        self.output_name()
+            .and_then(|name| state.niri.output_by_name_match(name.as_ref()).cloned())
     }
 }
